            <ArticleTitle>Osteoid osteoma of olecranon process of ulna in subchondral location.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 15-year-old girl with osteoid osteoma in an unusual subchondral localization of the olecranon. Unspecific complaints and minimal X-ray findings at the onset of the disease led to an incorrect diagnosis and more than 2 years of inefficient treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
